            @* Save and Cancel, not "Close".
               Until 2026-09-04 this footer held ONE button reading "Close", and closing is what
               committed: the button saved, Escape saved, and clicking the backdrop saved. The
               dialog two keystrokes away — Properties — has the identical wiring and DISCARDS on
               Escape, and nothing in either told you which you were in. Cody's rule, and it is
               now the rule for every dialog in the app: <b>Escape closes and discards</b>, and a
               dialog that can save says so on a button.

               `id="settings-close"` stays on the Cancel button: it is the id the browser
               harness's focus contract and ModalRoute both name, and it is still the control
               that closes without consequence. *@
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button id="settings-close" @onclick="Cancel"
                        aria-label="Cancel, close settings without saving">Cancel</button>
                <button class="primary" id="settings-save" @onclick="Save"
                        aria-label="Save settings and close">Save</button>
            </div>
        </div>
